//? Title: Xiaolin Wu's Line Algorithm: How Two Pixels Share a Line
//? Subtitle: Linear interpolation, endpoint weights and AirPassengers at two raster resolutions
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A line between pixel centres usually passes between rows or columns.
Wu's two-pixel antialiasing splits ink between the two adjacent centres.
We derive the split from conservation of weight and first moment, distinguish
it from exact area coverage, and account for fractional endpoint columns.
The existing full-column API is retained alongside an explicit clipped
endpoint policy. The built-in `air_passengers` dataset supplies a real
polyline: rendering it at two small resolutions shows both the benefit
of fractional weights and the information a small raster cannot preserve.
)

\toc

> The data: a monthly airline series

`dm::datasets::air_passengers()` contains 144 monthly observations from
1949 to 1960. `passengers` is the number of international airline passengers
in thousands. The frame stores year and month separately; a calendar index
puts successive records one unit apart. The increasing level and seasonal
peaks are features of the observations, not consequences of antialiasing.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/wu_airline_data.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto air = dm::datasets::air_passengers() | dm::mutate("time", [](const auto& r) {
    return r.get_double("year") + (r.get_double("month")-1)/12;
  });
  std::print("{}\n",air.head(6).to_md());
  std::print("\n{}\n",(air | dm::group_by("year") | dm::summarise(dm::agg::n("months"),
      dm::agg::mean("passengers","mean_thousands"),dm::agg::max("passengers","peak_thousands"))).to_md(3));
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create().line(air.get_column("time").values(),air.get_column("passengers").values(),
      "monthly data",dm::RGB{37,99,235},2)
      .title("AirPassengers: the original 144 monthly observations")
      .x_label("year").y_label("passengers (thousands)").size(1000,460).save_svg("build/wu_airline_data.svg");
}
```
